  <h2>Describe planning without turning vocabulary into advice</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>A <span class="ex">budget</span> is a plan for money coming in, going out, and being kept for later. To <span class="ex">track spending</span> is to record or review where money goes. To <span class="ex">save up for something</span> is to accumulate money toward a goal. To <span class="ex">cut back on something</span> is to reduce it, not necessarily stop it.</p>
  <p>A <span class="ex">loan</span> is money provided under an agreement to be repaid. The amount originally borrowed can be called the <span class="ex">principal</span>. <span class="ex">Interest</span> is an additional amount charged for borrowing under the stated rate and time conditions. An <span class="ex">installment</span> is one payment in a series. <span class="ex">Debt</span> is money or another obligation owed. These definitions help you understand and compare stated terms; they are not a recommendation to borrow, invest, or choose a product.</p>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You matched a plan, spending record, gradual savings goal, and deliberate reduction to the action stated in each fictional record.">
    <h3>Choose the planning action the sentence actually describes</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Money planning choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="set a budget">set a budget</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="track spending">track spending</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="save up for">save up for</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="cut back on">cut back on</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The fictional club plans how much can go to rent, supplies, events, and reserves next month. It will <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="set a budget" data-hint="Choose the action of creating a plan for stated inflows, outflows, and reserves." data-fix="The club will set a budget for next month.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The treasurer records every purchase and groups it by category. This helps the club <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="track spending" data-hint="Choose the action of recording and reviewing where money goes." data-fix="The purchase record helps the club track spending.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The club keeps $75 each month toward a projector it plans to buy later. It is trying to <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="save up for" data-hint="Choose the phrasal expression for accumulating money toward a named future goal." data-fix="The club is trying to save up for a projector.">choose</button> the projector.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>To reduce one optional category, the club changes weekly deliveries to monthly deliveries. It will <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="cut back on" data-hint="Choose the phrasal expression for reducing rather than necessarily ending an activity." data-fix="The club will cut back on deliveries.">choose</button> deliveries.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Sound natural: Make the amount and transaction role audible</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Keep the stressed syllable clear in <span class="ex">MON-ey</span> /ˈmʌni/, <span class="ex">BUD-get</span> /ˈbʌdʒɪt/, <span class="ex">SAL-a-ry</span> /ˈsæləri/, <span class="ex">ex-PENSE</span> /ɪkˈspɛns/, and <span class="ex">af-FORD</span> /əˈfɔrd/. The <span class="ex">p</span> is silent in <span class="ex">receipt</span> /rɪˈsit/, and the <span class="ex">b</span> is silent in <span class="ex">debt</span> /dɛt/. Common U.S. pronunciations of <span class="ex">interest</span> include /ˈɪntrəst/ and a fuller /ˈɪntərest/.</p>
  <p>Link function words in <span class="ex">Can_I_borrow...?</span> /kənaɪ ˈbɑroʊ/ and <span class="ex">Could_you_lend...?</span> /kədʒə ˈlɛnd/. The strongest stress follows the correction: <span class="ex">The <b>PRICE</b> is $480, but the <b>TOTAL</b> is $538.40.</span> Keep <span class="ex">thirteen</span> and <span class="ex">thirty</span> distinct: thir-<b>TEEN</b> commonly has final prominence in a contrast, while <b>THIR</b>-ty begins with the stressed syllable. Clarity matters more than copying one accent.</p>
